<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alalia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Aleria</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alalia was a Greek colony on the east coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corsica">Corsica</a>, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phocaeans">Phocaeans</a> around 565 BCE, on the site of modern Aléria. Refugees from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phocaea">Phocaea</a> reinforced it after the Persian conquest, and around 540 BCE their fleet fought a combined Etruscan and Carthaginian navy off the coast, the Battle of Alalia, after which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greeks">Greeks</a> abandoned the island. It later became a Roman colony, Aleria.</p></div>
